agents/architect.md adapts ideas from pstack's architect skill (grounding first,
designing twice, the design red flags), by Lauren Tan, licensed under the MIT License.

Source:      https://github.com/cursor/plugins/tree/main/pstack/skills/architect

The prompt rail (src/lib/promptRail.ts, src/components/PromptRail.tsx) takes ideas from
oikon48's prompt-rail Claude Code plugin, Copyright (c) 2026 oikon48, licensed under the
MIT License: a rail of the person's prompts with a thick tick for the one being read, the
turn line's form ("1m 23s · 2 edits · app.ts", up to three files written, two files with
one name told apart by their folder), and the search rule (the newest prompt holding every
word). The code was written for this project, except fileNames in src/lib/promptRail.ts,
which follows the plugin's function of that name closely.

Source:      https://github.com/oikon48/prompt-rail/tree/main/plugins/prompt-rail

src/lib/plainQuestion.ts (the plain-text question test) and server/explain.ts (the
explanation's four sections, the quoted-data instruction and the bounds on what is
sent) adapt qa-guide from claude_qamods, Copyright (c) 2026 aieo-product, licensed
under the MIT License.

Source:      https://github.com/aieo-product/claude_qamods/tree/main/plugins/qa-guide
